---
/* The atlas, drawn the way the home hero draws its runner: a field of hairline
   vertical strokes, the continents being where the strokes are. Pure vector —
   the path data was generated once from Natural Earth land polygons (50m,
   Natural Earth I projection, Antarctica, the high-arctic archipelagos and
   islands under 50,000 km² left out, slivers under 3px dropped) by scanning a
   vertical line every 4.5px across a 1440px-wide plate and keeping the runs
   that cross land. The viewBox is cropped to the land itself, so the
   continents run edge to edge of the band. Two densities of the same drawing:
   the 4.5px field above the phone breakpoint and a 9px one below it, where
   the fine pitch scaled to a phone would close up into a grey fill. Colour,
   weight and the swap live in the map-spread block of style.css. The path
   data itself lives in world-map.ts, shared with the home page's
   Architectural Influence card. */
import { MAP_VIEWBOX, MAP_FINE, MAP_COARSE } from './world-map';
---
<svg class="world-map" viewBox={MAP_VIEWBOX} fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
  <path class="world-map__field is--fine" d={MAP_FINE.d}/>
  <path class="world-map__field is--coarse" d={MAP_COARSE.d}/>
</svg>
